Z||000000||Cheever2||03-30-2001||08:50 PM||||Friends, I have seen the Forum membership double in the short time I've been here.  Whenever F.O.L.D. is mentioned, sometimes even our veterans say "Huh?".  So for their benefit, but especially for the new worshippers of the Plastic Miracle from Pontiac, I wish to bring to your attention the <B>F</B>iero <B>O</B>wners <B>L</B>ocation <B>D</B>atabase, or <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/cgi-local/foldinstructions.htm" TARGET=_blank> <B>FOLD</B> </A> for short.  I don't know who started it, but it's a great invention that can be very useful if we all pitch in to keep it as up-to-date as possible.  <P>I did a search and printed out the owners in my area, and keep that list in my car so that if I break down on the road I can hopefully call somebody to get advice or maybe a spare part.  Much better than being at the mercy of some Goober at the corner service station (if you can find one).  If I plan a trip, I look up owners who may be on the route, and contact them to see about dropping in or meeting up.  I contacted the Gold Coast folks that way, and they have since joined the Forum.<P>If you see an ad for a Fiero you like in a strange place (Utah, for example) you could find someone to ask if they can take a look or get some info for you.  <P>The people on the list won't be as familiar to you as Forum members, but you can never have too many Fiero owner contacts.  The list does have some old information in it, but if the 2,176 members here will sign up and keep the info current, it can be a valuable resource.  So click the link above and get into the FOLD!<P>I thank you once again for your support.<P>||||reg||6
